# Cloudflare Pages security headers.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
# This file is copied verbatim into the build output (out/) and applied by
# Cloudflare's edge. It has NO effect on GitHub Pages — it's Cloudflare-only.
#
# Most specific path wins. The Content-Security-Policy is shipped in
# Report-Only mode first so it can't break the GoHighLevel chat widget, hosted
# forms, or GA before it's been validated against real traffic. The allowlist
# below reflects what the live console actually reported: GHL uses BOTH
# leadconnectorhq.com and msgsndr.com; its widget pulls fonts from
# fonts.bunny.net; GTM/widget scripts need 'unsafe-eval'; and the background
# videos load from R2 (*.r2.dev) via media-src.
#
# To ENFORCE once the console is clean: (1) rename `Content-Security-Policy-
# Report-Only` to `Content-Security-Policy`, and (2) re-append `; upgrade-
# insecure-requests` to the policy (it's a no-op in report-only mode — it was
# removed here because report-only logs it as an error).

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.leadconnectorhq.com https://*.msgsndr.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://*.leadconnectorhq.com https://fonts.bunny.net; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://images.unsplash.com https://*.leadconnectorhq.com https://*.msgsndr.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.bunny.net https://*.leadconnectorhq.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.leadconnectorhq.com https://*.msgsndr.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com; media-src 'self' blob: https://*.r2.dev; frame-src 'self' https://*.leadconnectorhq.com https://*.msgsndr.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://*.leadconnectorhq.com https://*.msgsndr.com; object-src 'none'

# NOTE on the builder embeds (/embed/*): they're framed same-origin by our own
# product pages, which the global `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` + CSP
# `frame-src 'self'` already allow — so no override is needed here. (An earlier
# /embed/* rule that set `X-Frame-Options: ALLOWALL` produced a SECOND, conflicting
# X-Frame-Options header, which browsers reject → the iframe showed "refused to
# connect".) If third-party partner embedding is ever required, drop X-Frame-Options
# globally and control framing with CSP `frame-ancestors` per-path instead.
